{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"implementation_semantics\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"When a replica starts phase 1 for an instance owned by another replica (the recovery-led case) with Durable enabled, the metadata recorder must be given the record of that instance, and the call must not dereference a record the recovering replica does not hold.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\",\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Recovery-led startPhase1 on the captured snapshot: Durable true, the recovering replica is not the instance owner, and its own row holds no record at that instance number.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the recovering replica's row has no instance at that number, which is the state after a restart\\\",\\\"the recorder is enabled through the Durable flag\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"what the durable log contains when the recovering replica's row does hold an instance at that number, which the check does not exercise\\\",\\\"the launched configuration, which passes durable=false\\\",\\\"the later recovery rounds\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"startPhase1 writes the new instance into InstanceSpace[replica][instance] and then records metadata for InstanceSpace[r.Id][instance], its own row. In a recovery-led phase 1 the owner and the leader differ, so that slot belongs to a different instance or to nothing at all; the recorder dereferences the record it is given, so the call either persists the wrong record or terminates on a nil one.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Applies whenever phase 1 runs for another replica's instance with recording enabled, which is the recovery path that restarts phase 1 (sub-cases 5 and 6 of the prepare resolution).\\\",\n  \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"whether the same wrong-row write occurs when the recovering replica's row happens to hold that instance number\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}\nb10={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startPhase1\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":751,\\\"end_line\\\":779,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Phase-1 entry: it installs the new instance under the owner's row and records metadata for the recovering replica's own row.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The recording call indexes InstanceSpace by r.Id rather than by the instance owner, which is the discrepancy the check observes.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: with Durable enabled, does a recovery-led startPhase1 record metadata for the instance it is writing, or does it dereference the recovering replica's own row? Prefix: the harness creates a stable store, builds a replica whose own row is empty at that instance number, and calls the real startPhase1 with the owner different from the replica id. Controls: the prerequisite prints the durability flag, the recovering replica id and whether its own row holds the record, and the result prints the panic, the value and which rows hold instances afterwards.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that runs the real startPhase1 for another replica's instance with recording enabled and reports whether the metadata call terminates.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: the Replica is constructed in-package, the stable store is a harness temp file, and startPhase1 is called directly with the owner's coordinates instead of through the prepare resolution\\\",\\\"the harness wraps the call in recover() to observe a panic; production runs it inside the prepare path\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"leader_row\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"durable_phase1_prepared\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"durable\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"own_row_record_present\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The call is the one the prepare resolution makes for sub-cases 5 and 6 (startPhase1 with the recovered command), and the empty own row is the state of a replica that has not held that instance.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Durable true, recovery-led phase 1, empty own row.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the slot-exists case is not exercised\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-phase1-record\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-phase1-record\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"durable_phase1_result\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports whether the recording call terminated and where the instance landed, which is the duty's observable.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The recording was enabled and the instance belonged to another replica.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"leader_row.instance\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"leader_row\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-phase1-record\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"durable_phase1_result\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"panicked\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Recording metadata for a recovery-led phase 1 must not dereference a record the replica does not hold.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the case where the recovering replica's own row does hold an instance at that number is not exercised, so the wrong-row recording is only implied by the source\\\",\\\"the durable path is inert in the shipped configuration, so the consequence is bounded to callers that enable it\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":11,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"With Durable enabled and phase 1 started for another replica's instance, does the metadata recorder receive the record of that instance, or does it dereference the recovering replica's own row (which need not hold an instance at that number) and terminate the call?\\\",\n \\\"importance\\\":\\\"The recorder is the only place that persists acceptor metadata, and the recovery path that restarts phase 1 is exactly when persisting matters. Recording the wrong row would put another instance's ballot context into the log, and dereferencing an absent record terminates the replica; the consequence is bounded here because the shipped configuration passes durable=false, so this is an implementation-semantics duty owed by the recorder rather than a failure of the default deployment.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\",\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S2-instance-bookkeeping\\\",\\\"S24-runReplica-epaxos\\\"],\n \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"Durable true reached through the constructor argument\\\",\\\"recovery-led phase 1: the instance belongs to another replica\\\",\\\"the recovering replica's own row has no record at that number\\\"],\n \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"startPhase1 installs the new instance under the owner's row\\\",\\\"the recording call indexes the recovering replica's own row\\\",\\\"the recorder dereferences the record it was given\\\"],\n \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A2\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B9-recovery-trigger\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F7-durable-bytes\\\"],\n \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B2-phase1-attributes\\\":\\\"the phase-1 entry that makes the recording call\\\",\\\"B15-durable-record\\\":\\\"the recorder under test\\\"},\n \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"preservation\\\",\\\"priority\\\":1,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: startPhase1 writes InstanceSpace[replica][instance] and then records metadata for InstanceSpace[r.Id][instance], so the two coordinates differ whenever the leader is not the owner (S8-handlePropose-startPhase1)\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the run: the local construction run with Durable true and an empty own row reports panicked true with a nil pointer dereference while the owner's record was installed\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the shipped configuration: run.go passes durable=false, so this path is inert in the default deployment (S24-runReplica-epaxos)\\\"],\n \\\"unknowns\\\":[\\\"whether the slot-exists case records another instance's metadata, which the source implies but the check does not exercise\\\",\\\"whether any caller enables recording in practice\\\"],\n \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"This is the A2 recovery relationship at the durability boundary: the record that must survive is the one for the instance whose context is being changed by the recovery-led phase 1, which the recording call indexes through the recovering replica's own row instead.\\\"}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"New obligation and its first check for a second defect in the recorder's use: with Durable enabled, a recovery-led phase 1 records metadata through the recovering replica's own row, which need not hold the instance at all, and the recorder dereferences what it is given. The harness calls the real startPhase1 with the owner's coordinates and an empty own row and observes the nil dereference; the owner's record is installed, so the failure is in the recording call rather than in the instance setup. The consequence is bounded to callers that enable recording (the shipped configuration does not), and the slot-exists case is left as an explicit unknown.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-phase1-record.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_durable_row_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and binding are supplied with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; the duty is that the recorder receives the instance whose metadata is being written.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"question\\\":q,\\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b10]}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-phase1-record.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-phase1-record.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-phase1-record.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
